    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud said in his UN General Assembly address that Somalia requires continued international military support to combat al-Shabaab and stabilize the country.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud addressed the United Nations General Assembly this week, stating that Somalia still requires the assistance of foreign military forces. The president's remarks came during the annual gathering of world leaders in New York.\n\nIn his speech, Mohamud emphasized that Somali security forces are not yet fully prepared to take over the fight against al-Shabaab and other armed groups. He called for sustained international backing, particularly from countries contributing troops to the African Union mission in Somalia.\n\nThe president's appeal comes as the African Union Transition Mission in Somalia (ATMIS) prepares to draw down its personnel by the end of 2024. The mission has been gradually handing over security responsibilities to Somali forces. However, concerns remain about the capability of those forces to hold territory recaptured from al-Shabaab.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the president's message underscores the continued fragility of security gains in the homeland. Many diaspora members have invested in rebuilding efforts and maintain close ties to family in Somalia. A prolonged foreign military presence could affect stability and influence decisions about return or investment.\n\nThe international community has spent billions of dollars on peacekeeping and military operations in Somalia over the past decade. While al-Shabaab has been pushed out of major cities, it still controls rural areas and conducts frequent attacks.\n\nPresident Mohamud's call for continued support reflects the reality that Somalia's own forces are still in a rebuilding phase. The coming months will be critical in determining whether the transition to full Somali-led security can proceed without major setbacks.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/madaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-oo-shaaciyey-in-somalia-u-baahan-tahay-taageerada-ciidamada-shisheeye/425898/",
